#!./tesh

# pj_equals reads two traces in the same process. With the flex
# reader, the global scanner/parser state of the first parse must not
# leak into the second one (it used to crash on exit, mix event
# definitions and continue the line count of the first file).
$ ./pj_equals --flex ../traces/user_fields.trace ../traces/user_fields.trace
> 1

$ ./pj_equals --flex ../traces/user_fields.trace ../traces/states.trace
> 0

! expect return 1
$ ./pj_equals --flex ../traces/user_fields.trace ../traces/undefined_event_gap.trace
> PajeDecodeException: Event has not been defined in (Line: 50, Fields: '5, Contents: '3 0.2 p1 STATE A')
> ./pj_equals, error during the parsing of the input file ../traces/undefined_event_gap.trace
